# RFC 061: normalise line endings to LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Without this, GitHub's windows-latest runners check text files out
# with CRLF (their default core.autocrlf=true), while the repository's
# own content -- and every Rust string literal comparing against it --
# is LF. RFC 056 and RFC 060 both assert byte-identical file content,
# and fixture files served or compared verbatim (e.g. crates/apimock/
# examples/config/tests/**) break the same way test-side: not because
# apimock behaves differently on Windows, but because the bytes it's
# handed differ before it ever runs. `eol=lf` makes checkout the same
# on every platform instead of special-casing every affected test.
* text=auto eol=lf
